NAME
    help - list shell builtins

SYNOPSIS
    help

DESCRIPTION
    Lists the shell's builtin commands only, and points to /bin (ls /bin) for
    the externalized programs. Append -? to any command for its usage; man <cmd>
    for a full page. See `man sh` for an overview of the shell itself - the
    builtins in full, plus pipes, redirection, wildcards, and $VAR.

SEE ALSO
    sh, man
